Audit of a Debian 13 VM: 17 controls

STATUS   ID       SEVERITY  CONTROL
FAIL     KRN-004  medium    ptrace scope restricted
         kernel.yama.ptrace_scope is 0, expected 1, 2 or 3
         Otherwise a compromised process can read the memory of your other
         processes, including secrets such as keys held by ssh-agent.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module kernel.sysctl
FAIL     NET-005  medium    IPv4 ICMP redirects not accepted
         ICMP redirects are accepted on new interfaces (default) and eth0:
         accept_redirects 1 in all and on each, forwarding 0 on each
         Accepted ICMP redirects change the server's routes, so a forged
         redirect can send its traffic through another machine on the local
         network.
         fix: not automated yet
FAIL     KRN-001  low       Kernel pointers hidden
         kernel.kptr_restrict is 0, expected 1 or 2
         Kernel memory addresses help an attacker aim a kernel exploit; hiding
         them from normal users makes that harder.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module kernel.sysctl
FAIL     NET-004  low       IPv4 reverse path filtering enabled
         reverse path filtering is not 1 (strict) or 2 (loose) on new interfaces
         (default) and eth0: rp_filter 0 in all and on each
         Reverse path filtering drops incoming packets whose source address the
         server has no route back to, which stops many spoofed packets.
         fix: not automated yet

13 passed, 4 failed (2 medium, 2 low), 0 unknown
vps-ready can fix 2 of the 4 (KRN-004, KRN-001): run `sudo vps-ready plan`.
The other 2 need a manual fix for now; each says so above.
Run `vps-ready audit --all` to list the 13 passing controls too.
